---
import CtaRow from "../components/CtaRow.astro";
import {
  buyingLede,
  enterpriseModulesNote,
  functionsNote,
  laterModulesFollow,
  lightScheduler,
  paymentIntent,
  seo,
  trialNote,
} from "../content/copy";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title={seo.buying.title} description={seo.buying.description}>
  <h1>How buying works</h1>
  <p>{buyingLede}</p>
  <p>First accounts are created by hand.</p>
  <CtaRow />

  <section>
    <h2>What you buy</h2>
    <p>
      Project Modules, by the named seat. A customer buys a quantity of seats in
      a module. An administrator assigns each seat to one person. A seat is the
      licence to reach that module, reading included. Losing the seat removes
      the module, reading included.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What is for sale now</h2>
    <p>
      Only {lightScheduler.name} seats are for sale now. {lightScheduler.summary}{" "}
      {laterModulesFollow}{" "}See the <a href="/product">product page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What you do not buy</h2>
    <p>{enterpriseModulesNote}</p>
    <p>{functionsNote}</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How Santan intends to charge</h2>
    <p>{paymentIntent}</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Account shape</h2>
    <p>Chosen at sale, separately from modules.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Shared tenancy with row-level security. The Beta is joint tenancy,
        multiple logins, one Santan account.
      </li>
      <li>Dedicated database if a customer needs it.</li>
      <li>
        A FedRAMP deployment inside an Assured Workloads boundary is designed,
        not authorized, not this service, not for sale now.
      </li>
      <li>
        Customer-operated on the customer’s infrastructure is not the first
        release.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Trial</h2>
    <p>{trialNote}</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>AI</h2>
    <p>
      Both credit and bring-your-own-key will stand; credits first when they
      exist. Quantities are unset. Credits are not built. The Beta uses the
      customer’s own key. If the customer uses their own key, their contract
      with that vendor governs.
    </p>
    <p>
      AI is the only thing ever metered. A hard stop can only stop the
      Assistant, never the schedule.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  ul {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
  }

  li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }
</style>
